-- title:
--   Local unit index [R^×:(R^×)ⁿ]=#μₙ(R)·#(R/nR)
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is an integral domain and a discrete valuation ring, assumed complete with respect to the adic filtration by powers of its maximal ideal $\mathfrak m =$ `IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R`, and whose residue field $R/\mathfrak m$ is finite; the relevant algebraic and typeclass assumptions are carried as instances. Let $n$ be a natural number whose image $(n : R)$ is nonzero (which in particular forces $n > 0$). Consider the monoid endomorphism $u \mapsto u^n$ of the unit group $R^\times$, written `powMonoidHom n`. The assertion is an equality of natural numbers: the index in $R^\times$ of the range of this endomorphism, i.e. of the subgroup $(R^\times)^n$ of $n$-th powers, equals the product of the cardinality of `rootsOfUnity n R`, the subgroup of $\zeta \in R^\times$ with $\zeta^n = 1$, and the cardinality of the quotient ring $R / (n)$, where $(n)$ is the ideal generated by $(n : R)$. Cardinalities are taken as `Nat.card`, so the statement implicitly records that both factors, and hence the index, are finite and nonzero.
--
--   This is the classical local unit index formula for a complete discrete valuation ring with finite residue field, in the form valid for all $n$ invertible or not (wild $n$ included). It is used to count the $n$-th power classes of units in the completions of the ring of integers of a number field, via [`NumberField.natCard_units_adicCompletionIntegers_quotient_range_powMonoidHom`](thm.html#NumberField.natCard_units_adicCompletionIntegers_quotient_range_powMonoidHom).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsDiscreteValuationRing_index_range_powMonoidHom_units_eq.lean

